<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE II</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative analysis for conditioning on single modalities.<span id="S4.T2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> SR and Prog. indicate the success rate and the partial progress towards the goal, respectively. “SR<sup id="S4.T2.8.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.T2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">S</span></sup>” averages over simple experiments without obstacles. “SR<sup id="S4.T2.8.1.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.T2.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">C</span></sup>” averages over complex experiments with obstacles in the environment. Behavior indicates the success rate in following OOD language prompts.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
